; Picture $01: Bilbo's hall (Bag End)
;
; Header: border colour, attribute used to fill the screen (both replaced by 0
; when $95ED says it is dark); a stream of commands follows.  $08 x y: move the
; pen to x,y (start x=$7F, y=$3F).  Line, 2 bytes: 1 rrrr L U V / rr nnnnnn:
; V=1 vertical-major else horizontal-major, U=1 up (y decreases) else down, L=1
; left else right (L applies to the minor axis when V=1 and to the major axis
; when V=0); n+1 steps along the major axis; the minor axis moves once every
; r+1 major steps, r a 6-bit number (4 bits of byte 1, 2 bits of byte 2).
; Fill, 3 bytes: $40+ink, x, y: flood fill with that ink colour ($8071).
; Attribute paint, 3 bytes + runs: $20+paper, then the start attribute address
; (high byte first, $58xx), then runs cc cc cc dd (count-1 in the upper 6 bits,
; direction dd: 0 up, 1 right, 2 down, 3 left, one attribute cell per step)
; ending in $FF; each cell gets that paper, its ink inverted if it was equal to
; the paper.  $00 ends the picture.
@label=Picture01
